PHASE 3 — REST API (full CRUD + settings PUT/POST)                         [DONE]
================================================================================

  Goal: complete the stub handlers in tealkit_server.dart and add write
        endpoints so the Flutter GUI can manage tasks and settings via HTTP.

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/tasks
        - Parse JSON body, validate required fields (title, cron_expression,
          llm_prompt), return created task as JSON
        - Use uuid for new task ID

  [DONE] PUT /api/v1/tasks/<id>
        - Partial update; only fields present in body are overwritten

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/tasks/<id>/run
        - Trigger immediate one-off run; returns 202 Accepted with run_id
        - Runs via ServerTaskRunner.runTask() in an unawaited Future

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/tasks/<id>/cancel
        - Signal cancellation token for in-progress run

  [DONE] GET /api/v1/tasks/<id>/output
        - Return last output file content as {run_id, text, timestamp}

  [DONE] PUT /api/v1/settings/llm
        - Accept JSON, save via ServerLlmSettingsService.save()

  [DONE] PUT /api/v1/settings/data-sources
        - Accept JSON, save via ServerDataSourcesService.save()

  [DONE] PUT /api/v1/settings/preferences
        - Accept JSON, save via ServerPreferencesService.save()

  [DONE] GET /api/v1/settings/external-tools
  [DONE] PUT /api/v1/settings/external-tools

  [DONE] GET /api/v1/scheduler/log?limit=50&offset=0
        - Paginated read of scheduler_log table

  [DONE] Shared helpers:
        - _parseJsonBody(Request) → Map<String, dynamic>
        - _jsonError(String msg, {int status}) → Response
        - Input validation + 400 responses

  [DONE] dart:convert jsonEncode() replacing hand-rolled _toJsonString

================================================================================
PHASE 4 — MCP Proxy Routes                                                 [DONE]
================================================================================

  Goal: expose MCP tool calls over REST so the GUI (or external scripts) can
        invoke tools through the server without spawning their own child
        processes.

  [DONE] GET  /api/v1/mcp/servers
        - Lists GitHub MCP servers (DB) + selected external tool servers
        - Includes status (running/stopped), transport (http/stdio), tool_count

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/mcp/servers/<server_id>/start
        - GitHub MCP: HTTP or stdio transport auto-detected from envVars
        - External: ServerMcpClient over HTTP
        - Caches client/process in _mcpProxyClients / _mcpProxyProcesses

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/mcp/servers/<server_id>/stop
        - Disposes and removes client/process from cache

  [DONE] GET  /api/v1/mcp/servers/<server_id>/tools
        - Returns MCPTool list from running client or cached stdio tools

  [DONE] POST /api/v1/mcp/servers/<server_id>/tools/<tool_name>/call
        - Body: { "arguments": { ... } }
        - Routes to HTTP client or stdio process; returns MCPToolResult JSON

  [DONE] GET  /api/v1/mcp/servers/<server_id>/events (stdio only)
        - SSE stream forwarding stdout lines from child process
        - Returns 400 for HTTP-based servers

================================================================================
PHASE 5 — Scheduler                                                        [DONE]
================================================================================

  Goal: background cron-style scheduler that checks due tasks every minute
        and triggers ServerTaskRunner.

  [DONE] server/lib/scheduler/server_scheduler.dart
        - Timer.periodic(Duration(minutes: 1), _tick)
        - _tick: query all enabled tasks where next_run <= now()
        - For each due task: unawaited ServerTaskRunner.runTask(task)
        - After run: db.updateExecution (recordRun success/failure)
        - Avoid concurrent runs of the same task (track in-progress set)

  [DONE] Wire scheduler into serverBootstrap() in tealkit_server.dart
        - Start after all services ready
        - Graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM

  [DONE] cron_utils.dart (already exists)
        - Verified nextCronFire() correct for all supported expressions
        - Unit tests: server/test/cron_utils_test.dart (12/12 passing)

  [DONE] Retry logic
        - Exponential backoff (4 << attempt, clamped to 120s)
        - recordRun(success: false) on permanent failure

